{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2996","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2996","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2996\",\"parent_revision\":\"3555dd34a75452cc4fcf052b15cbe775e7b8e890669f77b1b9cd60ca95fe4b75\",\"root_revision\":\"3555dd34a75452cc4fcf052b15cbe775e7b8e890669f77b1b9cd60ca95fe4b75\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis session produced at least six distinct instances of an agent writing an unverified attribution or reference-existence claim into a human-visible surface (PR comment, GitHub issue body, or direct chat response) that was later found to be wrong when actually checked \u2014 each caught only by the user, not by any tool or process step:\\n\\n- \\\"SECTION_HEADING entries are display-only\\\" (PR comment, retracted)\\n- \\\"`example-argument-substitution` is a real caller of `parse.mjs`\\\" (retracted)\\n- Original #2985 framing: \\\"`backlog_update` silently discards description changes\\\" (rewritten after checking audit-comment evidence that was available the whole time)\\n- An unqualified \\\"human owned issue body\\\" citation presented with more confidence than the source document itself carried\\n- \\\"Opened PR #2988... fully closes the sessions.md injection instance\\\" \u2014 stated as fact before checking whether the PR's own CI had passed\\n- \\\"a script line I added in PR #2981 (get-gate-token.mjs)\\\" \u2014 `git blame` showed the line was added by an unrelated commit three months earlier; the PR's diff shows it only as unchanged context\\n\\nThe last four occurred in this exact session, after the first two had already been identified and discussed as a pattern \u2014 meaning awareness of the failure mode did not prevent its recurrence. CLAUDE.md already documents relevant countermeasures (`/hallucination-detector:hallucination-audit`, `citation-requirements.md`, `fact-verification-first.md`), but none of them are structurally required before a write to an external-facing, hard-to-retract record \u2014 they are opt-in disciplines that have to be self-applied under time/speed pressure, and did not fire in any of the six cases above.\\n\\nAt least a meaningful subset of these (\\\"X is/isn't referenced by Y\\\", \\\"I added/changed X in commit/PR Y\\\") are mechanically decidable by `grep`/`git blame`/`git log` before the claim is written, without requiring judgment. The broader class of architectural or causal characterization (\\\"this is deliberate design\\\", \\\"this silently discards data\\\") is not mechanically decidable the same way and would need a different treatment, if any.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **no mechanical check requires a reference-search citation before asserting \\\"x is/isn't referenced by y\\\" in an external-facing write** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Workflow-quality review, 2026-08-18/19; two further live occurrences observed 2026-08-19 within the same session that filed this item\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"cf395ec4edbc92f9b5e2e45a61a26d6321af01a951ed731c1181968ecc7c9db3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgvkMw\"}"}